stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PENDING: POST /orders, stock reserved
    PENDING --> CONFIRMED: PaymentSucceeded then reservation committed
    PENDING --> FAILED: PaymentFailed then reservation released
    PENDING --> CANCELLED: cancel request then reservation released
    CONFIRMED --> REFUND_PENDING: RefundPending event
    REFUND_PENDING --> REFUNDED: RefundCompleted event
    CONFIRMED --> REFUNDED: RefundCompleted with no prior RefundPending

    note right of PENDING
        Created only after catalog-service reserves stock via Feign.
        A reservation that is never paid is released by the scheduled
        expiry sweep, not by an order-status change.
    end note

    note right of CANCELLED
        Intended behavior: if a payment settles successfully after this
        terminal state, the payment layer issues a full refund.
        Current code does not move a CANCELLED or FAILED order back to
        REFUND_PENDING or REFUNDED; the refund is a payment-side effect.
    end note

    note right of REFUNDED
        Terminal. Requires CONFIRMED or REFUND_PENDING as the source
        status in Order.refund().
    end note
